@title The Demo — Chapter Two
@bg hall
@mood calm

narrate The hall is warmer than it looks from outside. That is true of most halls,
and most people.

@card keeper
narrate The Keeper has kept this hall for thirty years. She has buried four dogs
and one husband, and she will tell you about the dogs first.

keeper warm "Sit. Eat. You can tell me your name or not."
wanderer neutral "Does it matter which?"
keeper dry "It matters to you. That's usually enough."

choice
* "Give your real name."                     => truth+2
* "Give a name that isn't yours."            => truth-1, flag:false_name
* [Truth 2] "Say why you're really here."    => truth+2, bonds+1, lore:the_hall
* "Say nothing. Eat the soup."               => conviction+1
end

@label d1_02_after
@mood hope
keeper neutral "There. Now we know each other a little, which is the most
anyone can ask on a first night."
narrate The fire settles. Outside, the road goes on being a road.

@ach the_long_table
@finish
